From 10d7b531e633d5b5c8317f7b6944bfa4817dd451 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:35:24 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] kcm_networkmanagement: status line, labelled
 Add/Configure, editor and NetworkManager reads after the first frame
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: List (connections) + editor, QtWidgets KCModule with a QQuickWidget list (docs/page-design.md section 8). Not
ported to QML: the editor is about 12 widget tabs plus VPN plugins; this commit reworks the list side and the start-up
only. Connection settings, NetworkManager calls and the editor are unchanged.

Moved / renamed (kcm_connections/qml/main.qml):
- A status line comes first: "Ethernet: Connected to X" from PlasmaNM.NetworkStatus (activeConnections), or "Not
  connected". It is created 50 ms after the page opens (Loader), because NetworkStatus reads NetworkManager again.
- "Add new connection" (icon only, bottom right) -> "Add Connection…" labelled button beside the search field
  (kcm_networkmanagement/AddNewConnection). "Configure" (icon only) -> "Configure…" labelled
  (kcm_networkmanagement/ConfigureButton). Forget and Export stay icon buttons with tooltip and now an accessible name
  (kcm_networkmanagement/ForgetConnection, onRequestExportConnection); both are also in the row menu.
- Empty editor side shows "Select a connection to see and change its settings." instead of nothing.
- Markers: the 12 touched or weak rows in qml, plus 92 weak rows in the editor .ui files, wizard, model and VPN
  plugin files (comments only; XML comments in .ui, // in C++). inventory/kcm-extra-sources.json got an entry for
  kcm_networkmanagement (libs/editor, libs/models, vpn) because the check only looked at kcms/kcm_connections;
  strict check: 517 rows, 0 lost (was 103 lost at baseline). inventory/relabel/kcm_networkmanagement.tsv (outer repo).

Speed (read from code, kcm.cpp constructor):
- Before the first frame it ran NetworkManager::networkInterfaces() (blocking GetDevices plus per-device properties) to
  compute useApMode, connectionFromArgs()/defaultConnection() (primaryConnection, listConnections), selectConnection()
  which built the whole ConnectionEditorTabWidget for the preselected connection, settingsNotifier() and requestScan().
- Now all of that runs in startDeferredWork(), started once the QQuickWidget has rendered its first frame
  (QQuickWindow::afterRendering, then a 0 ms timer; a 2 s timer is the fallback if no frame is drawn). useApMode starts
  false and is set when computed (only the hotspot dialog reads it). The editor is therefore built on selection,
  after the list is visible.
Not changed (needs the models to be made async, larger): KcmIdentityModel / CreatableConnectionsModel (probes every VPN
plugin, creatableconnectionsmodel.cpp) are still built with main.qml; the editor tabs still build all widgets at
selection (connectioneditorbase.cpp). After: pending, manager will measure.

HIG: HIG-001, HIG-005, HIG-006, HIG-017, HIG-019, HIG-020.

Not built yet. Uncertain: QQuickWidget::quickWindow() afterRendering firing for the offscreen window (the 2 s timer
covers it); anchors between the search field and the add button; PlasmaNM.NetworkStatus is QML_ELEMENT in
libs/networkstatus.h and used by the applet, but not yet by this KCM's QML module imports (same plugin).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
